    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "The base and height of a triangle are whole numbers and its area is 12. Find all values of the base and height.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(b,h)=(1,24),(2,12),(3,8),(4,6),(6,4),(8,3),(12,2),(24,1)$.",
      "worked": "Since $\\tfrac12 bh=12$, we need $bh=24$. A positive area requires positive base and height. The positive factor pairs, including both orders, are $(1,24),(2,12),(3,8),(4,6),(6,4),(8,3),(12,2),(24,1)$.",
